{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "2a931f95-a85a-5412-a205-3c750bebb02e",
  "Description": "Balls rain on a torus that comes from a volume.\n\n[VolumePrimitive] builds a level set and [VolumeToMesh] turns it into geometry. Connected to the Geometry input of a static [RigidBody], that geometry is the collider, triangle for triangle. Any volume works the same way, including one loaded with [LoadVdb].\n\nAKA: voxel collider, vdb, level set, mesh collider, static mesh\n\nTips\n- A static body with Geometry collides as the exact mesh; a dynamic one is wrapped in a convex hull.\n- A coarser VoxelSize gives fewer triangles and a cheaper collider.\n- A volume that changes rebuilds the collider, so animate it sparingly.",
